# Widget Rules

## Base Classes

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Riverpod only | `ConsumerWidget` |
| Hooks only | `HookWidget` |
| Both | `HookConsumerWidget` |
| Neither | `StatelessWidget` |

## Widget Structure

```dart
class FeatureView extends HookConsumerWidget {
  const FeatureView({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    // 1. Hooks
    final controller = useAnimationController();
    // 2. Providers
    final state = ref.watch(featureControllerProvider);
    // 3. Listeners
    ref.listen(featureControllerProvider, (prev, next) { /* side effects */ });
    // 4. Return widget tree — use separate widget classes for complex sections
    return Scaffold(
      body: const FeatureContent(),  // separate file: widgets/feature_content.dart
    );
  }
}
```

## One Class Per File

Every widget class lives in its own `.dart` file. When a section of the build tree
is complex, extract it:

```dart
// widgets/feature_content.dart
class FeatureContent extends ConsumerWidget {
  const FeatureContent({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) => Container();
}
```

## FORBIDDEN — Private Widget Classes

```dart
// NEVER — private widget class
class _MyPrivateWidget extends StatelessWidget { ... }

// GOOD — separate file
// my_widget.dart
class MyWidget extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```

## FORBIDDEN — Private Widget Methods

```dart
// NEVER — method returning Widget
Widget _buildBody() { ... }

// GOOD — separate widget class in its own file
class BodyContent extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```
